{
	"metadata": {
		"name": "Thruster-Based Docking",
		"description": "A general thruster-based docking demonstration. The Servicer starts about 10 m along-track from the Client, with the Client attitude rotated so its docking adapter initially faces the Servicer. Reaction-wheel pointing maintains docking alignment while an eight-thruster translation system flies a port-relative rendezvous to a 5 m standoff and then performs a slower alignment-gated closure to capture."
	},
